.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt INTEL_INFOFRAMES 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm intel_infoframes
.Nd View and change HDMI InfoFrames
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "SYNOPSIS"
.Bd -literal
     intel_infoframes [OPTIONS]
.Ed
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     intel_infoframes is a tool to view and change the HDMI InfoFrames sent by
     the GPU. Its main purpose is to be used as a debugging tool. In some
     cases (e.g., when changing modes) the Kernel will undo the changes made
     by this tool.

     Descriptions of the InfoFrame fields can be found on the HDMI and CEA-861
     specifications.
.Ed
.Ss "OPTIONS"
.Bd -literal
     -h, --help
            Display comprehensive help on the tool.
.Ed
.Ss "LIMITATIONS"
.Bd -literal
     Not all HDMI monitors respect the InfoFrames sent to them. Only GEN 4 or
     newer hardware is supported yet.
.Ed
.Ss "REPORTING BUGS"
.Bd -literal
     Report bugs on fd.o GitLab:
     <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/igt-gpu-tools/-/issues>
.Ed
.Ss "SEE ALSO"
.Bd -literal
     HDMI specification, CEA-861 specification.
.Ed
